      "part": "one-sided coordinate direction",
      "finding": "The hypothesis is X1(sample)<=X1(point)+L. Global model deviations add exactly 2L0. Inverse materialH monotonicity then controls H(point)/H(sample), and the same direction controls each fixed nonnegative E0(sample) power by E0(point). It does not use the reverse implication."
