    },
    {
      "part": "midpoint geometry",
      "finding": "For any r in [l,h] within the ambient interval, endpointDistance(r)<=2*endpointDistance((l+h)/2). Each min branch uses the correct corresponding endpoint inequality, including l=a or h=b."
    },
    {
      "part": "total sqrt/log coordinate",
      "finding": "log(d/e)<=d/e-1<=1 gives log(1/e)<=log(1/d)+1. Real.sq_sqrt' yields the needed upper bound even when the logarithm is negative; sqrt_le_iff then proves X1(e)<=X1(d)+1."
    },
